  "query_preview": "..\nMostly island-effect convection is seen across the Marianas this\nafternoon. Winds remain light and variable across Saipan, allowing\nthe convection to continue over the island, with locally heavy\nshowers possible for the next couple of hours. Otherwise, expect \nonly isolated showers through the night. Winds are strong enough to\npush most of the showers off to the north of Guam, with one\nthunderstorm developing right along the Guam and Rota coastal \nwaters border. Overall, expect a drier pattern across the CNMI over \nthe next several days, though the light winds do lend to the chance \nof another round of island convection for Saipan and, to a lesser \nextent, Tinian again on Thursday. For Guam, the effects of the \nmonsoon trough look to move into the waters and over the island at \ntimes through the weekend, along with a risk of thunderstorms. Heavy \nrainfall does not look likely over the next several days.",
